00:48:39.000 --> 00:49:14.000
think that's such a tremendous exaggeration. So Leopold, he thinks, well, when the railway is done, I can dream bigger with all my money. You know, we can push maybe the railway up to the valley of the Nile. We can have a railway that goes up to the Sudan and to Egypt. He starts putting feelers out to Gladstone, the British prime minister. Would you be interested in selling me Uganda? And he says to his courtiers, you know, Belgium is an up and coming country, Spain, Portugal, the hated Dutch, you know, they're decadent. We can move in on their colonies actually, you know, we should be thinking big, we should

